as we near the four year anniversary of  the one october shooting many are  already gathering to honor the 60 we  lost a small vigil was held outside  silver state health tonight to remember  those victims it's a dark day that no  one will ever forget but the end of a  years-long lawsuit marks another step  towards healing sasha loftis joins us  live from the healing garden with more  tonight  denise and brian the pain of that day is  still fresh but the attorney i spoke  with tonight hopes that that settlement  will bring some relief after so much  suffering  it just changes your whole life jackie  barron shares her struggles since the  one october shooting the terror she  faced and the memories still cinched in  her mind all of a sudden it just started  popping and people started running she  says nothing can bring she and other  survivors peace  but as friday marks the fourth  anniversary of the route 91 harvest  festival many can breathe a sigh of  relief as an 800 million dollar lawsuit  settlement from mgm resorts draws to a  close it provides them closure you know  i'm not suggesting that it's something  that any of them will forget attorney  robert eglet represented many of the  more than 4 thousand victims and  relatives who received compensation he  says two court approved judges evaluated  claims and awarded money based on five  tears including ptsd physical injuries  or death with amounts starting at five  thousand dollars it's over we don't have  to go through protracted litigation for  years eglet and his team hope many can  find comfort at the end of this chapter  time does not get away from it but  barron hopes we always remember the day  the world changed for everyone in las  vegas  eglet's team tells me all of the clients  that were named in the settlement in  relation to their firm have gotten their  settlement money except for a few that  are still dealing with logistical issues  reporting live downtown tonight sasha  loftis live local now
 

